{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"head -80 update.json; grep -n '083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0' update.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Review the retained three-peer execution and record the current answer to the batched ReadIndex question. The receipt completed without test failure and its two correlated comparisons were both violated. The analysis distinguishes the demonstrated context-association and completion failure from a stale-read safety claim, and preserves the controlled ordering and in-memory storage limits.\",\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@earlier-remote-read-not-completed\",\n      \"kind\": \"fact\",\n      \"statement\": \"In the exercised three-voter group, when two follower-originated ReadIndex requests with distinct SystemCtx values were queued and the later context was confirmed first, node 2 received a ReadIndex reply carrying node 3's context. Node 2's original admitted batch still existed at index zero after the real ReadyToRead index 4 was applied, and the later context-101 confirmation produced no context-correct reply.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Three real in-process Raft Peer handlers with bootstrap membership {1,2,3}; node 1 leader; node 2 and node 3 follower-originated ReadIndex requests with distinct contexts; the later context's heartbeat was delivered to node 3 and its confirmation returned to the leader before the earlier heartbeat reached node 2; the test-only in-memory ILogDB and controlled logical delivery order were used; production code was unchanged.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n        \"readindex-confirm\",\n        \"pending-read-addready\",\n        \"pending-read-applied\",\n        \"pending-read-gc\",\n        \"follower-readindexresp\",\n        \"node-process-ready\",\n        \"node-readindex-admission\",\n        \"systemctx-identity\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"c2848ac1c82f442ba305267049bbb53b\": [\n          2,\n          3,\n          4\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\",\n      \"experiment_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-experiment\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n        \"readindex-confirm\",\n        \"readindex-test-context\",\n        \"pending-read-addready\",\n        \"pending-read-applied\",\n        \"pending-read-gc\",\n        \"follower-readindexresp\",\n        \"node-process-ready\",\n        \"node-readindex-admission\",\n        \"systemctx-identity\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"c2848ac1c82f442ba305267049bbb53b\": [\n          2,\n          3,\n          4\n        ]\n      },\n      \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n      \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The current conclusion is a bounded liveness and client-contract defect for follower-originated ReadIndex requests, not a demonstrated stale-read safety failure. The retained execution admitted node 2's context {101,1002} as event 0 and node 3's context {202,2003} as event 1. Event 2 is a ReadIndex reply addressed to node 2 after node 3's confirmation; its response_ctx_low is node 3's context value, its response_log_index is 4, and leader_pending_after is zero. Event 3 shows node 2's original batch still exists but has index zero, while the real ReadyToRead index 4 was applied and completed_after_response is zero. Event 4 processes node 2's later context-101 confirmation and produces zero context-correct replies; completion remains zero. The source explains this without an unresolved intermediate link: readIndex.confirm returns all earlier queued requests with their original contexts, handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation substitutes the confirming heartbeat's Hint/HintHigh for the remote reply, and pendingReadIndex.addReady only updates the exact SystemCtx key. pendingReadIndex.applied completes only batches with a nonzero index not exceeding the applied index. The earlier queue entry was deleted by the later confirmation, so the later context-101 heartbeat cannot repair it. The request remains uncompleted after a valid applied index; the observed endpoint for this pending batch is the caller-supplied timeout path, although the harness did not wait for that interval. The reply's log index is 4, a later committed index, so the observation does not establish that a stale read value was returned. The existing read-index unit test expects earlier requests to retain their own contexts, which is consistent with the consumer requirement but does not exercise this remote batched ordering.\",\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"The confirming context returns earlier queued requests while preserving each request's own SystemCtx.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"Remote replies are tagged with the confirming heartbeat context instead of the queued request's context.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"A response with a nonmatching SystemCtx leaves the original pending batch at index zero and cannot complete it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"The exercised later-confirmation ordering produced a mismatched reply context and left the earlier read batch unready after the ready index was applied.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The source path that constructs this remote reply uses m.Hint and m.HintHigh; no re-tagging occurs between that send and node 2's consumer in the probe, and the delivered reply carried node 3's context.\",\n        \"The response log index was 4 and the ready index was 4, so the execution does not show a stale committed index or stale application state.\",\n        \"The late context-101 confirmation produced zero context-correct replies and completion remained zero.\"\n72:          \"entry_id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
